– Vertices of degree zero are not connected to any other node, they do not contribute to the network topology. – Vertices of degree one constitute the sole negative contribution to the percolation condition (1.27). No further path is available when arriving at a site with degree one. – Vertices of degree two act as intermediators between two other nodes. Removing vertices of degree two does not change the topological structure of a graph.
